WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.704
A team that has to carry results.

2
00:00:03.754 --> 00:00:06.157
A leadership team under pressure.

3
00:00:06.207 --> 00:00:09.354
An organisation that wants to move forward.

4
00:00:09.404 --> 00:00:14.366
Then it is not enough to look at
job titles and organisation charts.

5
00:00:14.416 --> 00:00:19.525
The real question is: where is the energy,
and where does trust stall?

6
00:00:19.575 --> 00:00:25.115
That is what the Leadership &
Team Energy journey makes visible.

7
00:00:25.165 --> 00:00:31.753
Not as a judgement about people,
but as a picture of how a team works today.

8
00:00:31.803 --> 00:00:38.930
The journey brings three things together:
leadership attention, relational trust, and team energy.

9
00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:45.082
That is how it becomes visible what this
team carries today, and what holds it back.

10
00:00:45.132 --> 00:00:48.572
The platform shows patterns, tensions and emphases.

11
00:00:48.622 --> 00:00:52.130
Where does leadership steer too hard, or too little?

12
00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:54.730
Where does collaboration run smoothly?

13
00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.646
Where does energy leak away?

14
00:00:56.696 --> 00:01:00.286
That conversation does not stay abstract.

15
00:01:00.336 --> 00:01:13.248
It leads to concrete choices: where support is needed, what calls for a
redistribution of roles, and which team calls for a different composition.

16
00:01:13.298 --> 00:01:18.912
What emerges is a well-founded picture of the team,
with language for what stayed vague before.

17
00:01:18.962 --> 00:01:20.462
Open to discussion for HR.

18
00:01:20.512 --> 00:01:21.654
Usable for managers.

19
00:01:21.704 --> 00:01:23.562
Relevant for the executive team.

20
00:01:24.362 --> 00:01:25.883
No diagnosis.

21
00:01:25.983 --> 00:01:26.921
No label.

22
00:01:27.021 --> 00:01:29.898
The decision stays with the organisation.

